(3591844, 496980, 62095, '<td valign="top">This is a really good shot IMO.  I think the only reason that you didn''t finish higher up the tree is because of what your first comment mentioned - you look at the shot and you can think a lot of things, but not many of those thoughts are "hair" related. Would have been interesting to see how this did in the free study.</td>', 'This is a really good shot IMO.  I think the only reason that you didn''t finish higher up the tree is because of what your first comment mentioned - you look at the shot and you can think a lot of things, but not many of those thoughts are "hair" related. Would have been interesting to see how this did in the free study.', '2007-04-29 06:13:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592110, 498973, 60915, '<td valign="top">Yay!!!</td>', 'Yay!!!', '2007-04-29 11:20:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592381, 499323, 60862, '<td valign="top">Neat shot.  I like the flower sun a lot.  I agree about needing to blur the bottom of the island a bit, but mostly I just think how intriguing it would be to see this as you''re walking along!</td>', 'Neat shot.  I like the flower sun a lot.  I agree about needing to blur the bottom of the island a bit, but mostly I just think how intriguing it would be to see this as you''re walking along!', '2007-04-29 14:25:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592389, 497448, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is such a good pet photo. I think the DOF and focus are perfect. Your dog is adorable and has such a loving expression. I love the light -- you managed to highlight the whites without losing the detail.</td>', 'This is such a good pet photo. I think the DOF and focus are perfect. Your dog is adorable and has such a loving expression. I love the light -- you managed to highlight the whites without losing the detail.', '2007-04-29 14:29:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592643, 498973, 61651, '<td valign="top">Coming late to the comment party on this winner, and I don''t have anything to add that hasn''t already been said over and over, except this: when it loaded on my screen I was so struck by it that I did not hesitate to click "10".  Congratulations.</td>', 'Coming late to the comment party on this winner, and I don''t have anything to add that hasn''t already been said over and over, except this: when it loaded on my screen I was so struck by it that I did not hesitate to click "10".  Congratulations.', '2007-04-29 17:08:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592687, 498634, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is fantastic and it looks to me like a great children''s book illustration (hope you don''t find that comparison insulting).  There''s a delightful whimsy to it - a wonderfully creative and OOB take on the challenge requirements!</td>', 'This is fantastic and it looks to me like a great children''s book illustration (hope you don''t find that comparison insulting).  There''s a delightful whimsy to it - a wonderfully creative and OOB take on the challenge requirements!', '2007-04-29 17:28:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592697, 497280, 61651, '<td valign="top">Creative take on Hair, and the "hairy" details are nice and sharp.  Would have preferred to see a lot less of the distracting dust particles, though.</td>', 'Creative take on Hair, and the "hairy" details are nice and sharp.  Would have preferred to see a lot less of the distracting dust particles, though.', '2007-04-29 17:31:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592710, 496980, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is an arresting shot, very nice close-up, and I like the added detail of what appears to be a bridge leading off into the background.  Not sure how well you achieved the challenge, as others have noted, the hair doesn''t seem to dominate as the "theme" of the image - but as an image, regardless of the challenge, I think it''s very well done.</td>', 'This is an arresting shot, very nice close-up, and I like the added detail of what appears to be a bridge leading off into the background.  Not sure how well you achieved the challenge, as others have noted, the hair doesn''t seem to dominate as the "theme" of the image - but as an image, regardless of the challenge, I think it''s very well done.', '2007-04-29 17:34:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592717, 497337, 61651, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a very interesting idea - if I''m reading it right you set up a comparison (by hair) of a son to his father - a very imaginative take.  I agree with your own assessment that it might have been more effective if their eyes were level with each other.</td>', 'I thought this was a very interesting idea - if I''m reading it right you set up a comparison (by hair) of a son to his father - a very imaginative take.  I agree with your own assessment that it might have been more effective if their eyes were level with each other.', '2007-04-29 17:37:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592721, 498940, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like how you framed this with the head at the upper left and the hair fanning out to fill the whole right side - I do find the whites a bit on the harsh side, though.</td>', 'I like how you framed this with the head at the upper left and the hair fanning out to fill the whole right side - I do find the whites a bit on the harsh side, though.', '2007-04-29 17:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592730, 499323, 61651, '<td valign="top">Quite Dali-esque.  Love the flower in the sky.</td>', 'Quite Dali-esque.  Love the flower in the sky.', '2007-04-29 17:43:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3592787, 498891, 61651, '<td valign="top">Very edgy and dramatic. It has a certain charm - definitely hair is the centerpiece, and the tattoo is a good choice, adds that little bit extra visual interest, draws you right to the hair (as if the color wasn''t draw enough!).</td>', 'Very edgy and dramatic. It has a certain charm - definitely hair is the centerpiece, and the tattoo is a good choice, adds that little bit extra visual interest, draws you right to the hair (as if the color wasn''t draw enough!).', '2007-04-29 17:59:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3593092, 498973, 32754, '<td valign="top">This is just a masterful work of art and photography; your creativity and vision cannot be denied.</td>', 'This is just a masterful work of art and photography; your creativity and vision cannot be denied.', '2007-04-29 21:02:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3593305, 497305, 38127, '<td valign="top">Hey Sean.. what a fun shot.. that wee face is awesome!! I''ve made faces like this before but never THAT good ;) lol <br/> <br/>first time I came across this shot was in Art''s folder (an edit he did of it) .. just realized its your photo and not his.. apparently I need to start reading the titles ;) .. Anyway.. great moment captured.. brought a huge smile to my face !!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-29 21:31:20.</i></td>', 'Hey Sean.. what a fun shot.. that wee face is awesome!! I''ve made faces like this before but never THAT good ;) lol  first time I came across this shot was in Art''s folder (an edit he did of it) .. just realized its your photo and not his.. apparently I need to start reading the titles ;) .. Anyway.. great moment captured.. brought a huge smile to my face !!', '2007-04-29 22:30:21.000000', '2007-04-29 22:31:20.000000', 0),
(3593487, 498973, 66635, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  Congratulations on your well-deserved blue ribbon!</td>', 'Beautiful!  Congratulations on your well-deserved blue ribbon!', '2007-04-29 23:51:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3594811, 498973, 52549, '<td valign="top">The more I look at this, the more I''m sure that it''s one of the most beautiful portraits I''ve ever seen.</td>', 'The more I look at this, the more I''m sure that it''s one of the most beautiful portraits I''ve ever seen.', '2007-04-30 07:30:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3595380, 498763, 27482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>I did not vote in this challenge but this is one of the images I would vote a 5.5 if it existed, wich means I think it´s above average but would probably most depend on how I thought it stacked up against the competition in the challenge.<br/> <br/>Personally I think you made a good choice to have it b/w, I do think I would have liked it better with stronger contrast though, the whole shot just seems to "gray" for my taste.  Lighting is not bad but could be better, seems a bit too harsh as it causes glare on the skin and also that harsh shadow from the nose, could you have used a bigger light source or perhaps put some powder on your skin to reduce that?  That way you still would have had all that texture of the skin but more evenly lit.<br/> <br/>I tend to not use my lenses at f16 or smaller as the image quality suffers a bit due to diffraction and while it´s hard to say from this web size version I think this shot would have been sharper taken at around f8-11.  <br/> <br/>I do like the framing/crop but I tried opening it in photoshop and rotated it 90 degrees counter clockwise and liked it a lot better that way, do like you are experimenting with different crops but this time I think normal would have been better.  I also like the black backround, adds some mystery to the shot.<br/> <br/>Kind regards from Iceland, Larus.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) I did not vote in this challenge but this is one of the images I would vote a 5.5 if it existed, wich means I think it´s above average but would probably most depend on how I thought it stacked up against the competition in the challenge. Personally I think you made a good choice to have it b/w, I do think I would have liked it better with stronger contrast though, the whole shot just seems to "gray" for my taste.  Lighting is not bad but could be better, seems a bit too harsh as it causes glare on the skin and also that harsh shadow from the nose, could you have used a bigger light source or perhaps put some powder on your skin to reduce that?  That way you still would have had all that texture of the skin but more evenly lit. I tend to not use my lenses at f16 or smaller as the image quality suffers a bit due to diffraction and while it´s hard to say from this web size version I think this shot would have been sharper taken at around f8-11.   I do like the framing/crop but I tried opening it in photoshop and rotated it 90 degrees counter clockwise and liked it a lot better that way, do like you are experimenting with different crops but this time I think normal would have been better.  I also like the black backround, adds some mystery to the shot. Kind regards from Iceland, Larus.', '2007-04-30 10:46:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3597415, 498634, 57032, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC,<br/> <br/>Wow! What a labour of love! I feel like I''m critiquing a painting rather than a photograph, which isn''t necessarily a bad thing. All photographs have an art component to some degree, and you have certainly conveyed your artistic side here. There are great colours, interesting textures, and good contrast in this image.<br/> <br/>The problem many had, I believe, is that it no longer appears to be a photograph. This is certainly a work of art (and a good one, in my opinion), but this is primarily a competition of photography. Although the pictures of the hair are your originals, they''ve been used as a texture to create a painting, not a photograph.<br/> <br/>With that being said, there''s not much technically lacking with this shot. Everything is crisp (except the outline of the tree bark along the trunk), and actually looks like a forest scene if you let your imagination run wild a bit. The tree is well-positioned, and the falling leaves are a nice touch.<br/> <br/>I can''t do much else to critique this image, since there aren''t many photographic elements beyond those I''ve already discussed. Artistically, this is stunning, so I can see why it scored as well as it did. Since this is a photography site, I can also see why it didn''t score even better.<br/> <br/>Overall, I like it!<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Geoff Ball</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, Wow! What a labour of love! I feel like I''m critiquing a painting rather than a photograph, which isn''t necessarily a bad thing. All photographs have an art component to some degree, and you have certainly conveyed your artistic side here. There are great colours, interesting textures, and good contrast in this image. The problem many had, I believe, is that it no longer appears to be a photograph. This is certainly a work of art (and a good one, in my opinion), but this is primarily a competition of photography. Although the pictures of the hair are your originals, they''ve been used as a texture to create a painting, not a photograph. With that being said, there''s not much technically lacking with this shot. Everything is crisp (except the outline of the tree bark along the trunk), and actually looks like a forest scene if you let your imagination run wild a bit. The tree is well-positioned, and the falling leaves are a nice touch. I can''t do much else to critique this image, since there aren''t many photographic elements beyond those I''ve already discussed. Artistically, this is stunning, so I can see why it scored as well as it did. Since this is a photography site, I can also see why it didn''t score even better. Overall, I like it! Regards,Geoff Ball', '2007-04-30 20:50:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3597460, 496981, 43298, '<td valign="top">WTF.<br/> <br/>5.5<br/> <br/>That''s nuts, theres some serious hair going on here. I don''t know what people are thinking.</td>', 'WTF. 5.5 That''s nuts, theres some serious hair going on here. I don''t know what people are thinking.', '2007-04-30 20:57:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3597464, 497524, 43298, '<td valign="top">Award winning hair whip right there.</td>', 'Award winning hair whip right there.', '2007-04-30 20:58:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3597496, 497882, 45524, '<td valign="top">I like this shot and am a bit amazed that it didnt score better. The focus the lighting and the composition make it a wonderful shot. I like the vibrant colors of the hair and the brush. Nicely done.</td>', 'I like this shot and am a bit amazed that it didnt score better. The focus the lighting and the composition make it a wonderful shot. I like the vibrant colors of the hair and the brush. Nicely done.', '2007-04-30 21:04:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3598607, 497448, 57032, '<td valign="top">Hi from the CC,<br/> <br/>What an expression! You captured the emotion perfectly. Colours are good, as is the contrast and depth of field. The mouth and important fur are in focus, and I assume the eyes are, too. Some might complain that the eyes are underexposed, but I would disagree; they are perfectly soulful, and help convey the mood. As for the rest of the dog, perhaps it could use some frontal lighting. However, all the detail is observable and there is no noise, so it''s certainly not mandatory. The background is sufficiently blurred to shift focus to the dog.<br/> <br/>I don''t have many negative things to say about this image. Perhaps a slight desat of the background? I''d say you met the challenge requirements, so I have no idea why you got a 1, some 2s, and so many 3s.<br/> <br/>This shot ranked lower than it should have, given the competition.<br/> <br/>Great job with this shot.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Geoff Ball</td>', 'Hi from the CC, What an expression! You captured the emotion perfectly. Colours are good, as is the contrast and depth of field. The mouth and important fur are in focus, and I assume the eyes are, too. Some might complain that the eyes are underexposed, but I would disagree; they are perfectly soulful, and help convey the mood. As for the rest of the dog, perhaps it could use some frontal lighting. However, all the detail is observable and there is no noise, so it''s certainly not mandatory. The background is sufficiently blurred to shift focus to the dog. I don''t have many negative things to say about this image. Perhaps a slight desat of the background? I''d say you met the challenge requirements, so I have no idea why you got a 1, some 2s, and so many 3s. This shot ranked lower than it should have, given the competition. Great job with this shot. Regards,Geoff Ball', '2007-05-01 00:38:47.000000', NULL, 0),
